Negative control for the listing's ACTIVE/CLOSED tab pair (AC1/AC2).

Points the CLOSED tab at the `neq` leaf — the ACTIVE tab's operator — so both
tabs narrow the collection the same way. The tab still exists, still carries its
label, still writes through `setCriteria`, and still puts a `status.code` filter
on the wire: only the OPERATOR is wrong, which is the whole of what separates
"my closed tickets" from "my open ones". A spec that finds the control, or reads
only that some status filter left, stays green through it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: `client-tickets-listing.spec.ts` — "AC2 the Closed tab puts
filter[status.code]=ticket_closed on the wire", and the swap case beside it.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/useClientTickets/client-tickets.presentation.ts b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/useClientTickets/client-tickets.presentation.ts
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/useClientTickets/client-tickets.presentation.ts
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/useClientTickets/client-tickets.presentation.ts
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@ export const tabsUischema: CriteriaTabsUischema = {
